rs killed.....","","","n12330806684"],["Shipwrecks of the Harbor Beach Area","history board","As much as Lake Huron has been an asset, it has also been a deadly force to reckon with. Ships have foundered in huge storm waves; collisions have occurred in thick fog and blinding snow and some ships simply left port never to be seen again....","","","n12330806683"],["Harbor Beach Lighthouse","history board","On October 25, 1876, a lighthouse was erected on the north side of the main entrance of the harbor. A light, visible for 3 miles, guided ships to the safety of the new Government Harbor of Refuge...","","","n12330806682"],["Judge James H. Lincoln","history board","The Lincoln family has a long history of public service and political association. James Lincoln’s grandfather, Lansing Edgar Lincoln, was in the Michigan Legislature. James Lincoln's father, Burr Lincoln, was the Commissioner of Agriculture....","","","n12330806686"],["Harbor Beach Harbor of Refuge","history board","After a large number of shipwrecks in the Upper Thumb area, the Federal Government, in 1871, selected Sand Beach (in 1899 Sand Beach was renamed Harbor Beach) as the best location for a new Harbor of Refuge. Construction of the breakwall began in 1873.","","","n12330806681"],["Vicki Keith","plaque","At 7 A.M. Sunday, July 17, 1988, 27 year old Vicki Keith departed from Harbor Beach on an epic swim across Lake Huron. Vicki swam on through July 17, July 18, and onward into the early hours of Tuesday, July 19th.....","","","n12330806685"],["Klondike School","ruins","","","","n357757863"],["Friendship Tower","monument","","","","w321405619"],["Ziolkowski - a bust of James Butler \"Wild Bill\" Hickok","memorial","","","","n7626979798"],["U.S.S. Maine Memorial","memorial","","","","n8238302426"],["Lookout Mill","ruins","","","","n1519896257"],["Stolen Kiss Apartments","monument","","","","n4679539419"],["Historic Potter's Field","memorial","","","","n4679539420"],["General Samuel D. Sturgis Statue","